### Implementierungs-Phasen

#### Phase 1: Core Pipeline Infrastructure
- [ ] `Turn` struct + Builder
- [ ] `PipelineStage` Interface + `Pipeline` Orchestrator
- [ ] `PipelineStage` Registry (Namen → Instanzen)
- [ ] Basis `Turn` Builder aus HTTP-Request

#### Phase 2: Provider Adapter Framework
- [ ] `ProviderAdapter` Interface definieren
- [ ] Base Adapter (gemeinsame Logik: HTTP-Client, Headers, etc.)
- [ ] NIM Adapter implementieren
- [ ] ZEN Adapter implementieren (Header-Forwarding, Client-Locking)
- [ ] NVIDIA Direct Adapter implementieren
- [ ] Provider Registry (Name → Adapter)

#### Phase 3: Middleware Layers
- [ ] Retry/Fallback Layer mit konfigurierbaren Policies
- [ ] Logging/Metrics Layer (Request/Response Logging, Latency, Tokens)
- [ ] Error Classification System (für Retry/Fallback-Entscheidungen)

#### Phase 4: Strategy & Routing Layer
- [ ] `RoutingStrategy` Interface
- [ ] Heavy/Cruiser/Scout/NIM-Primary Strategies
- [ ] Ship-State-Tracking (Model-Affinität, Load, Failure-History)
- [ ] Fallback-Entscheidungen basierend auf Ship-State

#### Phase 5: Response Assembly & Streaming
- [ ] `ResponseAssembler` Interface
- [ ] Streaming-Pipeline (Reader-Chaining für Chunks)
- [ ] HTTP-Response-Assembly (Status, Header, Body/Stream)

#### Phase 6: HTTP Frontend Integration
- [ ] Turn-Object Builder aus HTTP-Request
- [ ] Pipeline-Execution im HTTP-Handler
- [ ] Response-Assembly → HTTP-Response Writer
- [ ] Graceful Degradation / Error-Handling

#### Phase 7: Testing & Migration
- [ ] Unit-Tests für jede Pipeline-Stage
- [ ] Integration-Tests für komplette Pipeline
- [ ] Migration der bestehenden Provider (NIM, ZEN, NVIDIA)
- [ ] Shadow-Testing gegen alten Proxy
- [ ] Feature-Flag für schrittweise Migration

